# Data conversion between megabyte and terabyte

Verifies direct data conversion between megabyte and terabyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1MB to 0.0000TB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5MB yields 0.0000TB; backward, converting 1TB to 1000000MB preserves the integer representation across the integer coarser-to-finer scale, while 1.5TB yields 1500000.0MB. Tiny magnitudes round to four fractional digits.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1MB
print(forward_whole->to(TB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5MB
print(forward_fractional->to(TB))
backward_whole: int = 1TB
print(backward_whole->to(MB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5TB
print(backward_fractional->to(MB))

<<< stdout
0.0000TB
0.0000TB
1000000MB
1500000.0MB

<<< stderr
